-- title:
--   Odd weight: the Hecke algebra is a subsingleton
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number that is nonzero, let $k$ be an integer with $k$ odd, and let $S$ be an arbitrary set of natural numbers. Consider the complex vector space $\mathrm{CuspForm}\,(\Gamma_0(N))\,k$ of cusp forms of weight $k$ on the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$, and inside its $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphism algebra the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), defined as the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra generated by the set `heckeGenerators N k S`, namely by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$. The assertion is that this subalgebra is a subsingleton as a type: any two of its elements are equal. Equivalently, the Hecke algebra so defined is the zero ring, all its generators coinciding with $0$; no claim is made about the even-weight case.
--
--   This is the degenerate case of the Hecke algebra in odd weight, reflecting the vanishing of $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ for odd $k$ (because $-I \in \Gamma_0(N)$). It serves to dispose of odd weights in the statements about Galois representations attached to Hecke eigensystems of weight $2 \le k \le p+1$, which are cited downstream in [`GaloisRep.exists_inertia_eigenvector_tameCharacter_pow_of_theta_heckeT_eq_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_katz_of_eq_three`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_inertia_eigenvector_tameCharacter_pow_of_theta_heckeT_eq_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_katz_of_eq_three) and [`GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_three_le_of_eq_three`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_three_le_of_eq_three), so that only the even weights in that range carry content.
